From: qcom-vp maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm: implement Qualcomm AMUv1 activity monitors on TCG max

The genuine SM8850 kernel runs __cpu_setup at image offsets
0xc97736ec..0xc97736f8. It reads ID_AA64PFR0_EL1.AMU, finds the feature
present under the opt-in x-qcom-ids profile, and executes
`msr amuserenr_el0, xzr`. The pinned CPU model defines no AMUv1 system
register behind that identification claim, so the write takes an
Undefined Instruction exception at EL1. UEFI's stale nonsecure vectors
catch it, and the kernel parks before any console output.

Add a minimum functional FEAT_AMUv1 implementation under the existing
x-qcom-ids profile. It adds AMCR_EL0, AMCFGR_EL0, AMCGCR_EL0,
AMUSERENR_EL0, AMCNTENSET0/1_EL0, and AMCNTENCLR0/1_EL0. It adds four
architected AMEVCNTR0<n>_EL0 counters with their fixed AMEVTYPER0<n>_EL0
event words. It adds eight auxiliary AMEVCNTR1<n>_EL0/AMEVTYPER1<n>_EL0
pairs. Access control follows Arm DDI 0601. AMUSERENR_EL0.EN gates EL0
access and HCR_EL2.TGE picks the trap target. CPTR_EL2.TAM and
CPTR_EL3.TAM trap EL1/EL2 access. A write to a controlling register
outside AMUSERENR_EL0 takes an Undefined Instruction exception unless the
current EL is the highest implemented EL. That rule keeps counter enable
under firmware control, the same rule Arm specifies.

CPU_CYCLES and CNT_CYCLES count from QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL, the timeline
that already clocks the generic timer. CPU_CYCLES uses a declared 1 GHz
virtual core frequency. CNT_CYCLES uses the generic timer counter value.
INST_RETIRED counts retired instructions only when QEMU uses precise
icount. Without precise icount it has no source, so it retains the last
guest write and does not follow a clock. STALL_BACKEND_MEM and the
auxiliary counters also have no source, and each one retains the guest's
last write while disabled. docs/qcom/sm88xx/stubs.md records these source limits.
AMCFGR_EL0 and AMCGCR_EL0 move out of the trace-only qcom_ids_reginfo
array into the new AMU array. Their reported words do not change.

Source: Arm DDI 0601 (2024-03), AMCR_EL0, AMCFGR_EL0, AMCGCR_EL0,
AMUSERENR_EL0, AMCNTENSET0/1_EL0, AMCNTENCLR0/1_EL0, AMEVCNTR0<n>_EL0,
AMEVTYPER0<n>_EL0, AMEVCNTR1<n>_EL0, and AMEVTYPER1<n>_EL0.
https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0601/2024-03/

